This message is really intended for Kenny Ragoonaden (or anyone else 
interested in the resolution of the problem I was having configuring DCE for 
Windows and logging in).  I was unable to contact Kenny as email kept getting 
sent back.

Anyway, the 2 problems that I had were:  being unable to configure the product 
if I used a hostname rather than IP address for the 2 servers, and being 
unable to do a dcelogin after I finally got the product configured.  The 
solution to both was the same:
I am using FTP software's PCTCP product so I needed to add a line into the 
pctcp.ini file just under the pctcp jernel statement as follows:

host-table = c:\etc\hosts

This line points to the hosts file on the PC.  I still have an outstanding 
problem with starting the DTSD (which is the DTS server) on the PC, but have 
decided not to run a server on that platform anyway.

For those in the USA who bought the product, support appears to be provided 
from PC software support which is available at 1-800-9924777 and they are very 
helpful.  

Hope this is of some help to you all.

Regards Jaqui


