Hi, received a few responses on some DCE and Kerberos questions I had:

> 1) Is there a Macintosh DCE client available...

Yes, Open Environment Corporation in Cambridge MA has one. Check with Jaqui
Lynch at the Boston College. lynch@delphi.bc.edu

> 2) Is there a Macintosh V5 Kerberos V5 client?

The Open Computer Security Group has one. tims@ocsg.com

> 3) Can a V5 Kerberos client make use of a DCE server?

from Shawn Mamros:

A DCE security server can act as a limited-functionality Kerberos V5
tickit-granting server for Kerberos V5 clients. However, there are some
restrictions - last time I checked (a little over three months ago), the DCE
server doesn't support proxiable or forardable tickets for V5, nor can it
support providing V4-style tickets as the MIT server optionally can (if you
have V4 clients around). Also, the Kerberos V5 client can't make use of any of
the DCE authorization stuff - that requires DCE itself.

