Cc: 

This occurs because TeX assumes that max(integer) + 1 = -1.  This is
how they have decided to decrement counters.

Since they typedef long (64 bits on the alpha) to integer, and assume
that the max value of an integer is the max value of a 32 bit integer,
they instead add 2^32+1 to counters, rather than decrementing them by
one.  This can be remedied by typdef'ing integer to int.

Look for the file web2c-5.851d/lib/config.h, and change the typdef:
#define INTEGER_TYPE long
	to
#define INTEGER_TYPE int

If you want to be clean about it, slap this in in place of the typedef:

#if defined( __alpha)
#define INTEGER_TYPE int
#else
#define INTEGER_TYPE long
#endif

