Yes, xdvi and dvips is building fine.  TeX needs some modifications.
What I did was:


TeX-3.14:

  1. Edit site.h and change
        typedef long integer
     to
        typedef int integer

  2. I also undefined BSD.

(If you need Mf as well, do the following changes.)

  3. Edit mf/MFwindow/x11.c
     
     Add the following definitions at line 39:
        typedef struct
            {
            unsigned int res_width;
            unsigned int res_height;
            Pixel res_fg;
            Pixel res_bg;
            } mf_res_struct, *mf_res_struct_ptr;
        static mf_res_struct mt_res;
    
     In the mf_resources structure, change the following:
	(Cardinal)mf_width  to XtOffset(mf_res_struct_ptr,res_width)
        (Cardinal)mf_height to XtOffset(mf_res_struct_ptr,res_height)
        (Cardinal)mf_fg     to XtOffset(mf_res_struct_ptr,res_fg)
        (Cardinal)mf_bg     to XtOffset(mf_res_struct_ptr,res_bg)

     Now search for "XtGetApplicationResources" and change the second
     parameter to "(XtPointer)&mf_res".

     Immediately following "XtGetApplicationResources", add the
     following lines:
        mf_width=mf_res.res_width;
        mf_height=mf_res.res_height;
        mf_fg=mf_res.res_fg;
        mf_bg=mf_res.res_bg;

  4. Edit common/texmf.c.  At line 172, change "(long)" to "(time_t)".

  5. Follow the standard procedure to build TeX.


