Hello:

I am running DCE 1.2 on a network of machines that run AIX 3.2.4 and
AIX 3.2.5.   My master registry is located on one of the AIX 3.2.5
machines.  All other nodes run as DCE clients off the security server.
All the clients, but one, are located on the same LAN.  The remote
client is running three (router) hops away on another LAN.   This
configuration results in high latencies when the remote client attempts
to communicate with the DCE security server and other clients within
the LAN, and causes unfavorable timeout frequencies.

I am attempting to solve this problem by replicating both the security
server (registry) and the CDS on the remote node to reduce the latency
of lookups and authentication when using RPCs.  I know it is possible
to replicate the CDS however I have found no way of replicating the
security server under DCE 1.2.  I know that I should be able to create
slave replicas but neither the secd nor sec_create_db  commands provide
such options.

Has anyone out there done any replication?  More specifically,  has
anyone ever replicated the security service on my target platforms? If
so,  how is it done?  Does it really improve RPC performance? I have
decided to run everything in the same DCE cell since the remote node is
not secure enough for a master registry and multi-cell communication
further exacerbates the latency problem.

Thanks in advance for your help.  Please reply to this newsgroup or
directly to me through e-mail.

Regards,
Dex
