Alas, the release notes for the IBM DCE 1.2 product specifically state
that replication is not supported. You can use sec_admin on the AIX
host to talk to a replicated registry on a non-AIX host.

Replicating a registry is simple. It is done through an option in the
config script. The steps are: run sec_create_db -slave, run secd (the
slave will automatically pull down a copy from the master when it
starts up the first time). An acl_edit to alter the /.:/sec/replist
ACL needs to be done as well. I should point out that the config in
this case is the OSF's generic 'dce_config' - consult your vendor's
DCE to see exactly how it shakes out there.

Do not attempt to do this on an AIX host - it will not work. I have it
working between a SCO DCE box and an OSF/1 DCE box. It works fine with
no problems whatsoever.
